# Shemá — project members (OBT-524; docs/shema.md §6.9)
#
# The link from an account to the projects whose team it is on. Only the Admin writes it
# (`admin` granted in the `shema` app — not the installation's is_platform_admin). A project's
# roster is read by whoever reaches the project's region, by its own live members and by the
# Admin; anybody else gets the 404 of a project that does not exist. A live membership is the
# session's `equipe`, so a member with no role anywhere passes the PME's door to the two reads.
#
# Removing a member marks the row (removed_at, removed_by) and never deletes it; adding the
# same account again later makes a new row.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@token = paste-an-access-token-here
@projectId = afrikaans-kaaps
@userId = paste-a-user-id-here

### The roster: who is on the team now, and since which day
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{projectId}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The Admin adds an account — 201 with the member; 409 if already live; 422 if no such account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{projectId}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": "{{userId}}"}

### The Admin removes it — 204; the row stays, marked
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/projects/{{projectId}}/members/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The projects the caller is a live member of — [{id, languageName}]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/me/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
